<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ganzhou Uyghur Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">894 CE – 1028 CE (approx.) · capital Ganzhou</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Uyghur khaganate in the Hexi Corridor, founded by refugees from the fallen steppe empire, that controlled a key stretch of the Silk Road for over a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/uyghur-khaganate">Uyghur Khaganate</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mongolia">Mongolia</a> was destroyed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yenisei-kyrgyz">Kyrgyz</a> in 840, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> groups fled south and west. One group settled among the oases of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu-corridor">Hexi Corridor</a> and by the 890s had made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhangye">Ganzhou</a> (modern Zhangye) the seat of its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagans</a> ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> herders alongside Chinese, Tibetan and other townspeople, profiting from the horse and jade trade between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. They sent tribute missions to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/five-dynasties-and-ten-kingdoms-period">Five Dynasties</a> courts and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>, intermarried with the Cao rulers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/guiyi-circuit">Guiyi Circuit</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunhuang">Dunhuang</a> and sometimes fought them. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> largely replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manichaeism">Manichaeism</a> of the old khaganate.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Rising Tangut power closed in, and in 1028 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-yuanhao">Li Yuanhao</a>, later founder of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/western-xia">Western Xia</a>, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhangye">Ganzhou</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> remnants survived in the region; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugurs">Yugur</a> (Yellow Uyghur) people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> are commonly regarded as their descendants.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ganzhou-uyghur-kingdom.jpg" alt="Ganzhou Uyghur Kingdom" width="320" height="221"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guiyi_Circuit.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>894 CE – 1028 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ganzhou</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Manichaeism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Uyghur</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ganzhou Uyghurs, Hexi Uyghurs</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=961&amp;focus=ganzhou-uyghur-kingdom" aria-label="Ganzhou Uyghur Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7719 1228 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ganzhou Uyghur Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8039 1484L7400 770M8039 1484L7641 1054"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7400 770h0M7641 1054h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8039 1484h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8039 1484h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ganzhou. <a href="/atlas?year=961&amp;focus=ganzhou-uyghur-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
